# Retired shapes (issue #265 part 4): nothing reads a project/ checkout or
# symlink, a projects/ directory or .workspace-worktrees/ any more, and the
# stale-shape report (make validate, make dashboard) names any still on
# disk. They stay ignored so a machine that keeps one, or registers a root
# under projects/ (ADR-0016 decision 1), keeps a clean main checkout (make
# sync skips a dirty one). Both project forms are needed: `project/`
# matches a real directory but NOT a symlink; bare `project` covers the
# symlink.
project/
project
projects/

# The per-machine registry and per-project settings files
# (see .agent/projects.local.example).
.agent/projects.local
.agent/projects.d/

# Worktrees (workspace and project, see issue #25)
worktrees/

# Retired worktree location (see the retired shapes above)
.workspace-worktrees/

# Make stamp files (setup state tracking — see ADR-0007)
.make/

# Dev-tools virtual environment (pre-commit, linters)
.venv/

# IDE settings
.vscode/
*.code-workspace
.codex

# Generated Claude Code skills (regenerate with: make generate-skills)
.claude/skills/make_*/

# Claude Code harness runtime state (per-session lock files; ephemeral, never committed)
.claude/*.lock

# Per-machine Claude Code settings: `claude plugin ... --scope local` writes it (ADR-0018)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Agent Scratchpad (Temporary files and artifacts)
.agent/scratchpad/*
!.agent/scratchpad/README.md

# Agent Identity (Runtime-generated, not template)
.agent/.identity

# Retired shared project config (issue #265 part 4): no longer read; the
# stale-shape report names what is left in it. Still ignored, as above.
.agent/project_config.sh

# Machine-local settings: inbox and sit-rep run-record paths (issue #386;
# template at .agent/settings.local.example)
.agent/settings.local

.env

# Python cache files
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# ros-manifest git-backed extends cache (tools/ros-manifest, #267)
.ros-manifest-cache/

# CodeQL generated files
_codeql_detected_source_root

# Cross-model review artifacts (see #193)
# Regenerated each /review-code run; bloats PR diffs and recursively grows
# until it breaks Codex's 1MB context window. Patterns are suffix-anchored
# (-prompt.md / -findings.md) so a future tracked review-*-summary.md
# audit-trail file is not caught.
.agent/work-plans/*/review-*-prompt.md
.agent/work-plans/*/review-*-findings.md
